---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaButtons from '../components/CtaButtons.astro';
import { withBase } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="What Zo Creates" description="Plain Markdown you own: your real context areas, sources, current truth, tasks, decisions, relationships, and memory.">
  <h1>What Zo Creates</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Everything Zo builds is plain Markdown — readable files you own, in your Zo
    workspace. No database, no special software. Depending on the depth you pick,
    your brain can include any of the following.
  </p>

  <h2>The building blocks</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Context areas</h3>
      <p>Your own domains of life and work — not generic categories. A business, a job search, family logistics, a health plan, a research thread, a creative project. Whatever you named.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Sources</h3>
      <p>The evidence behind what you know: meeting notes, email summaries, docs, transcripts, links, rough notes, screenshots, copied context. Kept separate from truth, because evidence isn’t always right.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Current truth</h3>
      <p>The working summary you’re willing to act on now. Updated carefully — never silently rewritten from a raw source.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Tasks &amp; decisions</h3>
      <p>Next actions, plus the choices you’ve made with the reasons attached, so they don’t quietly reverse later.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Relationships</h3>
      <p>How things connect. A person works on a project. A client belongs to a business. A source supports a claim. At Pro depth, these become real graph edges.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Memory</h3>
      <p>What changed over time and should survive into future sessions — global, per area, per project, per relationship, or per workflow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Routing &amp; index files</h3>
      <p>So Zo reads the smallest relevant slice of your brain instead of the whole thing every time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Knowledge graph <span style="color:var(--muted)">(Pro)</span></h3>
      <p>Typed entities, provenance, open conflicts, and validation checks, with routed reads. Optional, and only if you want it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout--ok">
    <p>
      And nothing gets written until you approve the plan. Zo proposes the files
      and folders, explains what each one is for, and waits for your yes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>It compounds through small updates</h2>
  <p>
    The brain gets sharper every time you leave one thing behind after a useful
    session — any one of these counts:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>one source,</li>
    <li>one update to current truth,</li>
    <li>one task,</li>
    <li>one decision,</li>
    <li>one relationship,</li>
    <li>one memory entry,</li>
    <li>or, at Pro depth, one graph or provenance update.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>See the exact files per depth</h2>
  <p>
    The precise folder layout depends on the depth you choose.
    <a href={withBase('/depths/')}>See the folder trees for Starter, Beginner, Intermediate, and Pro →</a>
  </p>

  <CtaButtons />
</Base>
